## STEP 1 — DELTA

[CHANGED] docker-registry.docker.com — NXDOMAIN confirmed (DNS彻底死亡, not just unreachable)  
[CHANGED] auth.docker.com — reveals x-docker-app-version: v1287, x-trace-id, rate-limit headers, session cookies on every request  
[NEW] api.hub.docker.com — empty response body (no error, no content — potential ghost endpoint)  
[CHANGED] api.offload.docker.com — Cloudflare-fronted, empty response (no longer returning content)

---

## STEP 2 — PRIORITIZE

[PRIO emsisoft] api.emsisoft.com/swagger/v1.0/swagger.json — 7.15  
attack_surface: 8 | business_value: 6 | tech_exposure: 9 | gate_ease: 7 | cloud_surface: 3 | freshness: 4  
Reason: Full OpenAPI spec publicly exposed with example data including GUIDs, emails, workspace structure. No auth needed to read schema. API has write endpoints (POST /v1/workspaces) requiring API key — test key handling.

[PRIO docker] auth.docker.com — 6.40  
attack_surface: 6 | business_value: 7 | tech_exposure: 7 | gate_ease: 3 | cloud_surface: 7 | freshness: 6  
Reason: Auth gateway leaks internal version (v1287), trace IDs, rate-limit state, and sets session cookies on unauthenticated requests. Cookie flags (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax) present. Potential session fixation or version-specific vuln.

[PRIO posit] staging.posit.cloud — 5.90  
attack_surface: 6 | business_value: 6 | tech_exposure: 8 | gate_ease: 5 | cloud_surface: 7 | freshness: 4  
Reason: SPA catch-all returns 200 on /actuator/health, /debug, /metrics, /env, /swagger-ui.html — all serving same SPA HTML (client-side routing). Frontend-only, no backend misconfig. Lower priority now.

[PRIO coxautoinc] api.coxautoinc.com — 5.10  
attack_surface: 5 | business_value: 5 | tech_exposure: 5 | gate_ease: 2 | cloud_surface: 4 | freshness: 3  
Reason: Persistent 403 on all probes (param=admin, param=internal_ip, param=169.254.169.254). Auth gate is solid. Class may be dead unless param encoding bypass found.

---

## STEP 3 — HYPOTHESES

[HYP emsisoft] Emsisoft API schema leak enables IDOR via GUID enumeration  
class: IDOR  
asset: api.emsisoft.com/swagger/v1.0/swagger.json  
confidence: 55  
reasoning: The public swagger.json exposes example response schemas with workspace GUIDs, user emails, and permission arrays. If the API accepts GUIDs in path parameters without verifying caller ownership, an attacker could enumerate workspaces via /v1/workspaces/{guid}. The example shows "permissions": ["owner","admin"] — if this is reflected in real responses, privilege escalation paths may exist.  
evidence_needed: Confirm whether /v1/workspaces/{any-guid} returns data without a valid API key, or whether 401 is returned consistently.  
verify_steps:  
1. GET https://api.emsisoft.com/v1/workspaces (no auth) → expect 401  
2. GET https://api.emsisoft.com/v1/workspaces/e8bafe40-dbe9-4f37-9c4c-4f55a034286e (no auth) → expect 401 or 200  
3. Compare responses to determine if GUID-based access is gated  
impact: If unauthenticated access succeeds → read any customer's workspace data (devices, alerts, seat counts, emails). Severity: High. If blocked → no issue.  
testability: PASSIVE  

[HYP docker] Docker auth gateway session cookie manipulation  
class: AUTH  
asset: auth.docker.com  
confidence: 45  
reasoning: The auth.docker.com endpoint sets a dckr-sessid cookie on every unauthenticated request. The cookie value is base64-encoded JSON containing what appears to be session state. If the cookie is not server-validated (e.g., client-side session), an attacker could forge session tokens. The x-docker-app-version header (v187) could reveal version-specific behavior.  
evidence_needed: Decode the dckr-sessid cookie payload, test if modifying the cookie grants access to authenticated endpoints.  
verify_steps:  
1. Decode the base64 portion of dckr-sessid → analyze structure  
2. Send request to https://app.docker.com/admin with modified dckr-sessid cookie  
3. Check if response differs from unauthenticated baseline  
impact: If cookie is client-validated → session hijack. If server-validated → no issue. Severity: Medium-High if exploitable.  
testability: AUTH_HELPED  

